Replacing $(n-1)!$ in the density by the gamma function
$
  Gamma(alpha) = integral_0^oo ee^(-x) x^(alpha - 1) dif x,
$
extends the definition to a general shape parameter: for $alpha, lambda > 0$ we say $X ~ Gamma(alpha, lambda)$ when
$
  f(x) = (ee^(-lambda x) dot lambda^alpha dot x^(alpha - 1)) / (Gamma(alpha)) quad quad "for" x > 0.
$
